6.6.6 Testing Plan

   1. Unit tests for each algorithm: Flow assembly on crafted PCAPs, JA3 computa-
       tion against published reference hashes, threshold calibration, fusion rules and the
       enforcer’s allowlist, rate limit and back-off.

   2. Integration tests: Replay labelled PCAPs around the entire system on a test system
       and compare results to the label.

   3. Live attack tests: Involve launching each in-scope attack from the attacker side onto
       our test systems on the isolated test network.

   4. Performance tests: For latency, throughput and resource use (Table 5.7).

   5. Fault-injection tests: Each service is killed or frozen under load in each failure
       mode, and recovery time and traffic impact are recorded.

   6. Soak test: The system runs for at least one week on a real home network in alert-only
       mode to measure false positives before blocking is enabled.

6.6.7 Hierarchical Organisation of the Source Code

The source code is organised as follows:
